\newlabel{tab:gate_sensitivity}{{8}{18}{Gate threshold sensitivity on the eight pre-registered cells (\S \ref {sec:analysis:prospective}). The predictor and the outcome definition are both as pre-registered; only the threshold moves. Bold is the operating point used in the paper}{table.caption.13}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces Mitigation spectrum on ETTh2 forecasting. Methods ordered by representation preservation (CKA, $h{=}96$). LoRA preserves representations (CKA$\approx $0.98) while \emph  {improving} over zero-shot. Mean $\pm $ std; Forgetting\% = (fine-tuned MSE $-$ zero-shot MSE) / zero-shot MSE $\times $ 100. \textbf  {Two caveats on comparability, added in revision.} Forgetting\% divides by the single shared zero-shot printed in each horizon header, not by each run's own zero-shot; the anchoring and LoRA runs measure their own at $0.127$--$0.131$, so their figures here are inflated by $1.2$--$3.4$~pp. And the rows are not matched on training-set size: B and C use $n{=}500$ training samples while L2-SP, EWC and LoRA use $n{=}1000$ (the $n$ column counts seeds, not samples). Matched at $n{=}1000$, $h{=}96$, each against its own zero-shot: full fine-tuning $.936$/$+13.4$, L2-SP $\lambda {=}0.01$ $.939$/$+16.0$, L2-SP $\lambda {=}0.1$ $.965$/$+13.4$, EWC $.972$/$+14.9$, LoRA $.979$/$-9.2$. On that comparison L2-SP $\lambda {=}0.1$ ties full fine-tuning rather than losing to it, so anchoring is not uniformly harmful; the dissociation the table is cited for (CKA not predicting utility) is unaffected. Condition~D reads CKA $0.99996$ rather than $1$: it leaves \texttt  {in\_proj} and \texttt  {mask\_encoding} trainable, so it is a frozen-\emph  {encoder} control and not a strict freeze. Only condition~H (Appendix~\ref {app:strictfreeze}) is $1.0000$ by construction. Earlier versions of this table printed D as $1.000$, which rounded that distinction away.}}{19}{table.caption.15}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:mitigation_spectrum}{{9}{19}{Mitigation spectrum on ETTh2 forecasting. Methods ordered by representation preservation (CKA, $h{=}96$). LoRA preserves representations (CKA$\approx $0.98) while \emph {improving} over zero-shot. Mean $\pm $ std; Forgetting\% = (fine-tuned MSE $-$ zero-shot MSE) / zero-shot MSE $\times $ 100. \textbf {Two caveats on comparability, added in revision.} Forgetting\% divides by the single shared zero-shot printed in each horizon header, not by each run's own zero-shot; the anchoring and LoRA runs measure their own at $0.127$--$0.131$, so their figures here are inflated by $1.2$--$3.4$~pp. And the rows are not matched on training-set size: B and C use $n{=}500$ training samples while L2-SP, EWC and LoRA use $n{=}1000$ (the $n$ column counts seeds, not samples). Matched at $n{=}1000$, $h{=}96$, each against its own zero-shot: full fine-tuning $.936$/$+13.4$, L2-SP $\lambda {=}0.01$ $.939$/$+16.0$, L2-SP $\lambda {=}0.1$ $.965$/$+13.4$, EWC $.972$/$+14.9$, LoRA $.979$/$-9.2$. On that comparison L2-SP $\lambda {=}0.1$ ties full fine-tuning rather than losing to it, so anchoring is not uniformly harmful; the dissociation the table is cited for (CKA not predicting utility) is unaffected. Condition~D reads CKA $0.99996$ rather than $1$: it leaves \texttt {in\_proj} and \texttt {mask\_encoding} trainable, so it is a frozen-\emph {encoder} control and not a strict freeze. Only condition~H (Appendix~\ref {app:strictfreeze}) is $1.0000$ by construction. Earlier versions of this table printed D as $1.000$, which rounded that distinction away}{table.caption.15}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces The strict-freeze control (condition~H) beside condition~D on the six cells that met the degradation definition under the superseded trend baseline, plus ILI. B$-$H keeps B$-$D's sign on all seven cells. Generated by \texttt  {scripts/cell\_matrix.py --latex}.}}{19}{table.caption.17}\protected@file@percent }
